  "laegnaNotesSub4-theory": {

    "purpose":
      "These four notes are not additional audible notes. They are the reflected representation of the previous octave, allowing octave transitions to be represented continuously.",

    "relationship":
      "II→IE behaves to OI→OE similarly as logarithmic reflection behaves to explicit manifestation.",

    "hexadecimal-role":
      "Together with the 12 primary musical notes they complete the full Laegna hexadecimal 16-state musical space.",

    "hologram-role":
      "The reflected band provides continuity below octave origin and allows traversal through octave zero in linearized musical coordinates."
  }
